Implications
------------

* Non-commercial use only. Do not redistribute these clips in any commercial
  product or paid service.
* The NPZ is a derivative of the upstream CSV (forward-kinematics replay adds
  body poses + velocities). It is bundled here for research convenience under a
  best-effort attribution reading of the upstream license. Downstream users
  with stricter compliance needs should re-derive the NPZ from the original
  CSV via `scripts/convert.sh`.
* Attribution: cite Ubisoft LAFAN1 + the Unitree retargeting effort (see the
  HuggingFace dataset card) whenever you publish results trained on these
  clips.
* The csv_to_npz conversion script in `scripts/csv_to_npz.upstream.py` is a
  verbatim copy of `src/mjlab/scripts/csv_to_npz.py` from mjlab
  (https://github.com/Mujoco-Lab/mjlab), Apache-2.0 licensed.

Re-conversion
-------------

`scripts/convert.sh` documents how to regenerate the NPZ from a fresh CSV
download. It requires a one-off `uv pip install mjlab` and a working CUDA
device (mjlab's converter is GPU-only by default).
